course: dictionary
lesson: 5025
title: Ingenuity and clever ideas
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ingenuity means being clever and inventive, so you find new and smart ways to solve problems. The adjective is ingenious: an ingenious idea is a clever, new one.
explain: Look at the words around it. «NASA has landed rovers on Mars since 1997, and Perseverance, landing in 2021, brought the helicopter Ingenuity.» The sentence is about a clever machine, so it fits. Try your meaning in its place: "the helicopter's cleverness" makes sense.
explain: Phrases help too: «human ingenuity», «show ingenuity», «use your ingenuity». Each one praises smart thinking. When Ingenuity has a capital letter, it is also a name for a small helicopter that flew on Mars.
fact: Ingenuity means being clever and inventive, with new and smart ways to solve problems.
fact: Ingenious is the adjective: an ingenious idea is clever and new.
fact: Ingenuity is an uncountable noun, so you say «some ingenuity», not «an ingenuity».
fact: With a capital I, Ingenuity was a small helicopter flown on Mars.
fact: Ingenuity made the first powered flights on another planet.
exercise: «The rover Perseverance carried a small helicopter called Ingenuity, which flew on Mars.» What is Ingenuity in this sentence? | A planet | A type of Martian dust | *A small helicopter | A rover
exercise: What does ingenuity mean? | Being very tired after a long day | Being lost on a hill | *Being clever and inventive, finding smart ways to solve problems | A kind of rock on Mars
exercise: What is the adjective form of ingenuity? | glowing | ancient | *ingenious
test: «NASA has landed rovers on Mars since 1997, and Perseverance, landing in 2021, brought the helicopter Ingenuity, which made the first powered flights on another planet.» In this sentence, Ingenuity is | *the name of a small helicopter that flew on Mars | a planet far from Earth | a rover that landed in 1997
test: Which phrase best shows someone used cleverness to solve a problem? | *used their ingenuity | ran away from it | ate their lunch | slept through the problem
exam: Which sentence uses ingenuity correctly? | The ingenuity was a long walk home | *Her ingenuity helped her build a raft from old bottles | She ate ingenuity for breakfast
